MiniBang: About
================

What is MiniBang?
------------------

MiniBang is a minimal Arch Linux-based setup for older laptops with very low RAM
(~1GB), where a modern Arch install with Wayland and a full desktop environment
isn't practical. Built entirely with pacman and official Arch repositories — no
separate distro, no alternate package manager, no AUR.


Origin
------

MiniBang is a sibling project to ArchBang, sharing its archiso build tooling but
targeting the opposite end of the hardware spectrum. Where ArchBang runs MangoWM
on Wayland for modern machines, MiniBang strips back to Xorg + i3 for hardware
that can't carry a compositor.


Design Philosophy
-----------------

  * Lightweight - low overhead stack for ~1GB RAM hardware
  * Xorg, not Wayland - no compositor tax
  * No GTK/Qt - dmenu, i3bar/i3blocks, urxvt throughout
  * Arch underneath - full pacman access, official repos only


Stack
-----

  - Xorg (xorg-server, xorg-xinit, xorg-drivers)
  - i3 - tiling window manager, with i3bar + i3blocks built in
  - rxvt-unicode (urxvt) - daemon mode, one process shared across windows
  - feh - wallpaper
  - dmenu - app launcher
  - lf / links - terminal fallbacks for files/web (no GUI browser or file
    manager shipped by default)


Getting Help
------------

For Arch-related questions: https://wiki.archlinux.org

MiniBang is not affiliated with Arch Linux.

